      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "beta(2)-Adrenergic agonists are the most widely used bronchodilators for the treatment of asthma. On the other hand, there is concern that excessive use of beta(2)-agonists may contribute to the exacerbation of asthma. However, the mechanism of such adverse effects of beta(2)-agonists is not completely clear."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "The aim of this study was to assess the direct influence of beta(2)-agonists on airways by analyzing the effect of a beta(2)-agonist, fenoterol, on airway sensitivity in an animal model and on tachykinin neurokinin-2 receptor expression in bovine tracheal smooth muscle."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "We performed an acetylcholine challenge test on ovalbumin sensitized guinea pigs that were exposed to daily inhalation of ovalbumin and fenoterol. We also investigated the effects of fenoterol on neurokinin-2 receptor messenger RNA and density with Northern blot analysis and receptor binding assay."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULT",
          "content": "The increase of airway responsiveness and the decrease of beta(2)-adrenergic receptors were found in guinea pigs that were treated with fenoterol. There were time- and dose-dependent increases of neurokinin-2 receptor mRNA and of density in tracheal smooth muscle that was treated with fenoterol."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "This increased airway responsiveness, increased neurokinin-2 receptor expression, and decreased beta(2)-adrenergic receptor density may be relevant to asthma exacerbation."
        }
      ]},
